    19	Entire automatically scans transcript and metadata content before writing it to the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch. Three detection methods run during condensation:
    20	
    21	1. **Entropy scoring** — Identifies high-entropy strings (Shannon entropy > 4.5) that look like randomly generated secrets, even if they don't match a known pattern.
    22	2. **Credentialed URI detection** — Redacts connection strings and URLs with embedded passwords, such as `REDACTED`.
    23	3. **Pattern matching** — Uses [gitleaks](https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks) built-in rules to detect known secret formats.
    24	
    25	Detected secrets are replaced with `REDACTED` before the data is ever written to a git object. This is **always on** and cannot be disabled.
    26	
    27	### Recommendations
    28	
    29	If your AI sessions will touch sensitive data:
    30	
    31	- **Use a private repository.** This is the simplest and most complete protection. Transcripts on `entire/checkpoints/v1` are only visible to collaborators.
    32	- **Avoid passing sensitive files to your agent.** Content that never enters the agent conversation never appears in transcripts.
    33	- **Review before pushing.** You can inspect the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch locally before pushing it to a remote.
    34	
    35	## What Gets Redacted
    36	
